/* A win, composed onto ScreenScaffold. What is left here is the three things
 * neither the frame nor a component can know: that the stat cells sit in a
 * row, that the arrivals wrap, and that the headline is a sentence rather
 * than a label.
 *
 * TWENTY-THREE DECLARATIONS BECAME NINE IN PHASE 8 TASK 11 AND NONE OF THE
 * FOURTEEN WAS REPLACED BY A COPY HERE, which is the test of whether a screen
 * composes the layer or re-derives it:
 *   - the root's `padding: var(--gutter)` and `align-items: center` are the
 *     scaffold's content region, which puts the gutter on
 *     `unity-scroll-view__content-container` so an elevated card's shadow is
 *     not clipped at the viewport edge.
 *   - `__headline`'s size, weight and ink are `.t-hero` and `.t-success`.
 *     Both are single-class selectors in Theme.uss and `.t-success` is
 *     declared after `.t-hero`, so the green wins the colour and the 28px
 *     survives - which is the pairing `SpliceRevealView` already uses.
 *   - `__reward` is gone entirely: the reward is a StatCell now, so its size,
 *     its ink and its tabular face come from `t-num` and `.stat-cell__value`.
 *     Marking a Label by hand was the thing StatCell exists to stop.
 *   - `__granted`'s --green-tint fill, row radius, 12px padding and
 *     `width: 100%` are gone and nothing took their place. That panel drew a
 *     full-width green block behind a single 160px card, and a blank one on
 *     every wave that granted nothing. PostWaveView.Bind has the measurement.
 *   - `__grant`'s size, weight, ink and wrap were describing a Label that has
 *     not been in this tree since the grants became CreatureCards. The rule
 *     survives as the one line the card grid does need, which is the gap
 *     under a wrapped row.
 *   - `__next`'s top margin and full width are the CTA row's own padding and
 *     its `flex-direction: column`, and the button's whole treatment is
 *     Theme's `.btn-primary`.
 *
 * THE STAT ROW IS THIS FILE'S AND NOT StatCell.uss's. A cell carries half the
 * handoff's 8px gap on each of its own sides; the `flex-direction: row` that
 * puts two of them side by side belongs to whatever holds them, and a
 * component's stylesheet reaches its descendants and never its parent.
 * StatCell.uss's closing note records how that was found out.
 */
.post-wave-view { flex-grow: 1; }


/* A sentence, not a label, so it wraps - "Wave not cleared." fits on one line
 * at 28px on a 430 frame and a longer verdict from a later server would not. */
/* CENTRED AS TEXT, NOT AS LAYOUT. This screen's root used to carry
 * `align-items: center` and it was dropped on the claim that the scaffold's
 * content region supplies it. It does not - `.screen-scaffold__content` is
 * `flex-grow` alone and its content-container rule sets a gutter and a
 * `min-height` only, neither of which centres anything - so a short verdict
 * stretched to full content width and rendered flush left,
 * while SpliceRevealView, the third screen of the same beat, stayed centred.
 *
 * The fix is text-align rather than the container's `align-items`, because
 * this is a Label whose TEXT is off-centre, not a box in the wrong place.
 * Centring the content container instead makes every sibling shrink-wrap,
 * which collapses the stat row into overlapping cells - measured, in a
 * capture, before this was written. */
.post-wave-view__headline {
    white-space: normal;
    -unity-text-align: middle-center;
    margin-bottom: var(--space-3);
}

/* THE -4px IS `StatCell.uss`'s OWN PRESCRIPTION AND NOT A NUDGE. A cell
 * carries half the handoff's 8px gap on each of its own sides, because USS
 * here has no `gap` and no `:last-child`, and that file says what a caller
 * that wants the row flush does about it: "cancels it with a -4px margin on
 * the container, which is one line at the call site rather than a rule that
 * looks like it works and does not." Without it the row is inset 4px from the
 * card's padding on both sides. `DeployView.uss` and `WaveDefeatView.uss`
 * carry the same cancel for the same row; this screen was the one that did
 * not, which is a residual Phase 9 Task 18 closed rather than a new rule. */
.post-wave-view__stats {
    flex-direction: row;
    margin-left: -4px;
    margin-right: -4px;
}

/* The arrivals, laid out like RosterView's grid and for the same reason: a
 * CreatureCard is a fixed 160px, two of them plus the 12px gutter leave 406
 * of space for 320 of card, and `space-between` is what puts a pair against
 * both edges and an odd third at the left where the next row starts. */
.post-wave-view__granted {
    flex-direction: row;
    flex-wrap: wrap;
    justify-content: space-between;
    margin-top: var(--space-2);
}

.post-wave-view__grant { margin-bottom: var(--space-3); }
